The line of code with the error is expecting y2 to have 3 dimensions (y2[s,v,t]) but as you said it only has 2 in your data. Based on a quick look at the code it seems like your input data is organized in a long/vertical form [site * occasion, year] but the "calculating integrated likelihood" section of the JAGS code is expecting things organized as an array [site, occasion, year]. I'm not sure which way of organizing is the way you want it but I'd go back and check through each line of the JAGS model and make sure the dimensions are what you expect them to be.

Ken

